nodecode-voicestudio is a rewrite of aska-digital's aska-digital/protean-voice-studio:

  https://github.com/aska-digital/protean-voice-studio
  commit efe5c1910ee22de7e911a9c8a8625027781f2729
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 aska-digital (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the whole client, in Common Lisp over the cell's HTTP seam, with
the plugin's own routes and form fields -- /generate for a short take (text,
profile_id, speed, seed; the x-seed header and the server's own audio_path
answer both honoured), /setup/status and /profiles, /gallery/voices,
/archetypes and /personalities for the three kinds of voice, the design path
(/design/describe into /profiles with kind=design and vd_states) and the
clone path (/profiles with kind=clone and the recording as a file part),
/audiobook/plan, /audiobook, the server-sent progress stream it answers
(started, per-chapter, done) with the artifact fetched from /audio/<output>,
the job reads behind /jobs/<id> and the job lists, /audiobook/resume/<id>,
/batch/enqueue and /batch/jobs/<id>, and /dub/translate as the other door
for a dub. Also kept: the plugin's six tool names and its six --flag
commands (/vs-speak, /vs-design, /vs-voices, /vs-longform, /vs-dub,
/vs-status), its ceilings (6000 characters for a take, 2000 for a voice
description), the 0.25-to-4.0 pace, the wav/m4a sample and mp4/mov/mkv/
webm/m4v video allowlists, the chapter count and the refusal of markup a
voice cannot perform, the per-language dub result with the languages that
failed named, and the recovery lines -- the server unreachable, an unknown
voice, a duplicate name, an interrupted render to resume. Its reading of the
markdown script (# headings split chapters, ## stays body text) is the same.

Left out: Hermes' tool registry and the JSON envelopes the plugin answered
with -- the answers here are readable text naming the file, which is what a
chat surface shows; the plugin's bookkeeping under its own data directory,
since the audio is written under this cell's section folder instead; and the
module-level settings the plugin read once at register() time, which are this
cell's section.

Two hardening changes: an explicit out_path is a bare file name inside the
section's folder (the plugin allowed any path its own check accepted), and
the clone sample passes the same allowlist and location gate as every other
input file (the plugin checked only its extension). The VoiceStudio
application itself is not bundled: it is a separate desktop app, and this
cell only speaks to the server it runs.
